  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers NIST SP 800-63-4 Digital Identity Guidelines, final since 31 July 2025: the base volume (digital identity risk management, impact assessment, IAL/AAL/FAL selection, tailoring and the Digital Identity Acceptance Statement), SP 800-63A-4 (identity proofing at IAL1-3, evidence strength, validation, verification pathways, no KBV), SP 800-63B-4 (authenticators at AAL1-3, password length and blocklists without composition rules or forced rotation, MFA, phishing resistance, syncable authenticators, rate limiting, binding, account recovery, notifications, sessions and reauthentication) and SP 800-63C-4 (FAL1-3, assertion contents and validation, injection protection, holder-of-key and bound authenticators, shared signaling, wallets). It lists two version lines: SP 800-63-4 (current) and SP 800-63-3 (legacy, upgraded from). SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions and upgrades, assurance levels, identity proofing, authenticators, sessions and recovery, and federation.",
